From 59cafadadeb6164abec215ff98876e88333b8651 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 14:35:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/46] DucoBoxSerial: faster stuck-RH detection, tighter
 plausibility floor

Confirmed live 2026-07-18 via a direct serial capture across an actual
physical UC button press: a stuck valve raw RH sits bit-exact flat
while the valve is also pinned near 100% airflow, and its paired
control unit own independent RH sensor disagrees sharply (over 30
points) while stuck, then agrees closely once the reading unsticks.

Use both as corroborating signals to shorten the required flat
duration below the baseline 20 minutes: pinned-high airflow drops it
to 5 minutes, a disagreeing paired UC (via the network table asso
column, newly parsed in ParseNetworkRows) drops it to 3 minutes, with
neither weakening the existing 20-minute baseline when no
corroborating signal is present.

Also raise DUCO_MIN_HUMIDITY from 3 to 15: a known-dead sensor was
observed producing an implausible 4% reading that the old floor let
through as valid.

Signed-off-by: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>

Assisted-by: claude:claude-sonnet-5 [Bash] [Edit]
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [WIP]
---
 hardware/DucoBoxSerial.cpp | 90 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 hardware/DucoBoxSerial.h   | 17 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 99 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

